D3 Scale Chromatic and CELLXGENE compatibility
-----------------------------------------------

d3_rainbow and d3_cool reimplement the interpolateRainbow and interpolateCool
formulas from d3-scale-chromatic v1.5.0, commit
05e76dafaa89059153e177a4f57d9af985ba49a8:
https://github.com/d3/d3-scale-chromatic/blob/05e76dafaa89059153e177a4f57d9af985ba49a8/src/sequential-multi/rainbow.js

d3-scale-chromatic attributes interpolateCool to Matteo Niccoli's perceptual
rainbow. interpolateRainbow combines D3's warm and cool ranges as its cyclic
"less-angry rainbow". The d3_cool source vector contains the exact 100 bins at
t = 0:99 / 100; its priority order is reversed to reproduce CELLXGENE's
low-to-high continuous-data mapping. d3_rainbow dynamically uses
t = 0:(n - 1) / n, with a 200-color reference retained for registry audits.
The RGB conversion also follows d3-color v1.0.3 and d3-interpolate v1.1.6,
the versions pinned by CELLXGENE for this implementation; both are distributed
under the same BSD-3-Clause terms reproduced below.

The usage semantics are documented by CELLXGENE colorHelpers.js at commit
76a39fcf92da57c9e4fd59831ad805a3b007da8c:
https://github.com/chanzuckerberg/cellxgene/blob/76a39fcf92da57c9e4fd59831ad805a3b007da8c/client/src/util/stateManager/colorHelpers.js

